+| `create_file` with a path that holds `..`, such as `folder.root / ".." / "x.toml"`, and with a text that is not a `str`. | `DataFolder.relative` compares the parts of two paths and does not resolve `..` (F03 design 2.1), and every caller passes the paths that `DataFolder` gives. A text that is not a `str` breaks the type in the signature, which mypy checks. |
+| A process that is killed, and a PC that loses power, during `menu new`. | The removal cannot run then, and no test can stop a process at a chosen step. F11-T14 and F11-T24 check the case of Ctrl+C that acts like a killed process. |
+| A real Ctrl+C from a console, access that the file system denies, and a real second program that creates the file or holds it open. | No CI machine has a console, the root user on Linux ignores mode bits, and no test can time a second program to a step. The fault harness raises `KeyboardInterrupt`, which is what Python raises for Ctrl+C, as F05-T41 does. It also raises `PermissionError` and makes the race at the step that each case picks (section 2). |
+| Ctrl+C during `menu show`. | `cli` gives exit code 130 for every command (F05 design 2.10), and F05-T41 tests it. `menu show` writes no file, so Ctrl+C leaves nothing behind. |
+| `menu new` and `menu show` on a date near the last date of `datetime.date`. | F06-T22 tests `week_from_argument` there, and the PC's clock gives no such date (F06 design 2.7). |
+| The help with the eight commands of v0.1, with `shop`. | F05-T45 checks those lines with the stand-ins, and v0.1-S19 checks them with the real commands. F11-T01 checks the lines of `menu new` and `menu show` in a form that holds when F13 adds `shop`. |
+| Chinese output in Windows Terminal. | No CI machine has a Windows console (architecture 10), so v0.1-S25 has Troy check it. F11-T30 checks that the Chinese tables line up by display width, and F11-T36 checks that `python -m recipe_menu` writes the Chinese output as UTF-8. |
+| Doc comments are in English only. | R05. troy-check rejects Chinese characters in doc comments. |
+| The plans for later features in design section 2: F13's `shop` with `NO_MENU`, F14's `menu suggest`, and F15's `add` with `create_file`. | The design and the test plan of each later feature cover them. F11-T04 checks `NO_MENU` through `menus`, and F11-T10 checks the name `Rice.toml` that F15's case names. |
+| v0.1-S08, v0.1-S13 to v0.1-S16, v0.1-S23, and v0.1-S31 in the release test. | They are version tests in `version-tests/`, which the version tests PR adds (TE5). F11-T16, F11-T20, F11-T29, F11-T33, F11-T34, and F11-T35 run the same steps at `main`, and F11-T38 times the same command on the same kind of folder, in every test run. |
